        <h2>A nurturing environment for people to thrive</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="about-grid">
        <div>
          <p>Elysian Hope Foundation was started out of a desire to make a positive difference in the lives of vulnerable and less fortunate people in our communities. We saw children, families, and individuals facing challenges such as lack of basic necessities, food insecurity, inadequate sanitary products, and limited access to opportunity — and we wanted to respond.</p>
          <p>We believe that every person deserves dignity, hope, and an opportunity to live a better life. Our work is inspired by Christian values of love, compassion, service, and caring for others — bringing hope where there is need, empowering vulnerable communities, and inviting others to become part of creating positive change.</p>
          <p>We believe even small acts of kindness can make a meaningful difference in someone's life.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p>Founded by Junevillar Angose, the Foundation is registered with Kenya's NGO Co-ordination Board (NGO-KJUDKPB) and guided by a board of directors, currently active across Nairobi, Nakuru, Kiambu, Kajiado, and Vihiga counties.</p>
          <div class="stat-row">
            <div><strong>3</strong><span>Core program areas</span></div>
            <div><strong>5</strong><span>Counties of operation</span></div>
            <div><strong>2021</strong><span>Founded in Nairobi</span></div>
