        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Our founder's story</p>
          <h3 class="founder-name">Junevillar Lihanda Angose</h3>
          <span class="founder-title">Founder, Elysian Hope Foundation</span>
          <div class="founder-copy">
            <p>On 29th May 2020, at a young age, Junevillar Lihanda Angose took a step that would become the beginning of a much bigger journey. Driven by her faith in God and a genuine desire to serve communities, she founded Elysian Hope Foundation with a simple but powerful belief: kindness can change lives.</p>
            <p>Her desire to serve was deeply personal. Having witnessed how poverty can affect a person's dignity, opportunities, and hope for the future, Junevillar felt a strong conviction to do something for communities facing difficult circumstances. She believes that sometimes, a small act of kindness can be the encouragement someone needs to keep going.</p>
            <p>The foundation's journey began with a simple visit to a children's home. What started as one act of service gradually grew into a bigger vision to reach more children, families, and vulnerable members of society and remind them that they are seen, valued, and cared for.</p>
            <p>With the support of friends, family, and well-wishers, Elysian Hope Foundation continued to grow. Their generosity, encouragement, and willingness to serve alongside her helped transform a personal passion into an organization with a broader community impact — a journey that eventually led to the foundation's registration as an NGO.</p>
            <p>Today, Junevillar continues to champion a culture of compassion, community service, and hope. Her journey is a reminder that you do not have to wait until you have everything to make a difference. Sometimes, change begins with simply being willing to care.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="founder-quote">&ldquo;Kindness is better.&rdquo;</div>
